We need answer only DUT between [BEGIN] and [DONE]. Need implement TopModule. Spec: input scancode 16 bits, outputs left down right up. Map scancodes: e06b left, e072 down, e074 right, e075 up. Combinational always @(*) with case. Need avoid latches: assign defaults or full case with default. Outputs one bit. Need exactly module named TopModule. SystemVerilog. Could use always_comb. Let's craft.

Need consider "last two bytes of scancodes received": scancode 16 bits directly given. Just compare.

Implementation:

module TopModule (
    input  logic [15:0] scancode,
    output logic left,
    output logic down,
    output logic right,
    output logic up
);

always_comb begin
    left = 1'b0;
    down = 1'b0;
    right = 1'b0;
    up = 1'b0;
    case (scancode)
        16'he06b: left = 1'b1;
        16'he072: down = 1'b1;
        16'he074: right = 1'b1;
        16'he075: up = 1'b1;
        default: begin
            left = 1'b0;
            down = 1'b0;
            right = 1'b0;
            up = 1'b0;
        end
    endcase
end

endmodule

Could also use unique case? Not necessary. Some would use always @(*) reg? SystemVerilog logic fine.

Need ensure no latches: defaults set all outputs. Good.

Return [BEGIN] ... [DONE]. No explanation.

[BEGIN]
module TopModule (
    input  logic [15:0] scancode,
    output logic left,
    output logic down,
    output logic right,
    output logic up
);

    always_comb begin
        left  = 1'b0;
        down  = 1'b0;
        right = 1'b0;
        up    = 1'b0;

        case (scancode)
            16'he06b: left  = 1'b1;
            16'he072: down  = 1'b1;
            16'he074: right = 1'b1;
            16'he075: up    = 1'b1;
            default: begin
                left  = 1'b0;
                down  = 1'b0;
                right = 1'b0;
                up    = 1'b0;
            end
        endcase
    end

endmodule
